78,15.233L-53.141,15.847L-52.535,16.103L-51.983,15.981L-51.669,15.828L-51.58,15.991L-51.591,16.307L-51.765,16.43L-51.831,16.57L-51.718,16.798L-51.587,16.881L-50.934,16.598L-50.845,16.439L-50.945,16.244L-50.832,16.153L-50.739,16.193L-50.647,16.122L-50.425,16.238L-50.163,16.596L-50.144,16.826L-50.246,16.991L-50.166,17.272L-50.2,17.405L-50.089,17.371L-49.938,17.554L-49.469,17.761L-49.521,17.792L-50.079,17.647L-50.124,17.792L-49.904,18.109L-49.653,18.078L-49.17,18.235L-48.938,18.19L-49.247,17.889L-48.663,18.246L-48.849,19.53L-48.874,20.745L-48.452,21.345L-48.438,21.539L-48.506,21.682L-48.896,21.985L-51.072,23.051L-51.329,23.531ZM-50.716,15.72L-50.754,15.87L-50.754,15.711L-50.813,15.73L-51.016,16.135L-51.08,16.07L-51.058,15.914L-51.251,15.723L-51.317,15.702L-51.49,15.859L-51.579,15.789L-51.626,15.592L-51.551,15.341L-51.595,15.01L-51.454,14.957L-50.978,15.035L-50.856,14.957L-50.359,15.397L-50.716,15.72ZM-50.376,11.624L-50.725,11.459L-50.638,11.39L-50.202,11.394L-50.166,11.446L-50.376,11.624ZM-50.007,11.228L-49.929,10.993L-49.742,11.041L-49.76,10.885L-49.619,10.681L-49.447,10.735L-49.576,10.922L-49.427,11.065L-49.456,11.128L-50.09,11.429L-50.122,11.35L-50.007,11.228Z", "events": [{"year": -241, "title": "Battle of the Aegates", "text": "In March, the Roman fleet of Lutatius Catulus destroys Carthage's last relief fleet off western Sicily.", "lon": -45.519, "lat": 3.782}, {"year": -241, "title": "Peace with Rome", "text": "Hamilcar Barca negotiates the peace: Carthage leaves Sicily and must pay Rome 3,200 talents.", "lon": -44.529, "lat": 4.058}, {"year": -241, "title": "Gisco ships the army", "text": "From Lilybaeum, Gisco sends some twenty thousand mercenaries to Africa in batches, so each can be paid off in turn.", "lon": -45.1, "lat": 3.0}, {"year": -241, "title": "Unpaid in Carthage", "text": "Carthage, its treasury empty, lets the veterans gather in the city unpaid, then moves them out.", "lon": -53.18, "lat": -1.37}, {"year": -241, "title": "Sent to Sicca", "text": "The army, with families and baggage, is sent to wait at Sicca, far inland.", "lon": -59.316, "lat": -4.452}, {"year": -241, "title": "Hanno pleads poverty", "text": "Hanno the Great asks the soldiers to accept less than they were promised; they refuse.", "lon": -59.164, "lat": -4.544}, {"year": -241, "title": "March on Tunis", "text": "The mutineers march on Tunis and camp within sight of Carthage.", "lon": -53.752, "lat": -1.6}, {"year": -241, "title": "Gisco seized", "text": "Spendius, a runaway Campanian slave, and Mathos, a Libyan, turn the army against Gisco and take him prisoner.", "lon": -53.638, "lat": -1.738}, {"year": -241, "title": "Libya rises", "text": "Libyan towns, crushed by wartime taxes, send seventy thousand men; women give their jewellery to pay the army.", "lon": -56.115, "lat": -3.9}, {"year": -240, "title": "Utica besieged", "text": "Spendius lays siege to Utica, Carthage's oldest ally.", "lon": -54.171, "lat": -0.404}, {"year": -240, "title": "Hippo besieged", "text": "Mathos's men besiege Hippo Acra on the northern coast.", "lon": -54.895, "lat": 0.562}, {"year": -240, "title": "Hanno at Utica", "text": "Hanno's elephants rout the besiegers, but his careless army is surprised and loses its camp.", "lon": -54.324, "lat": -0.542}, {"year": -240, "title": "Hamilcar returns", "text": "Hamilcar Barca is given ten thousand men and seventy elephants.", "lon": -53.256, "lat": -1.232}, {"year": -240, "title": "Crossing the Bagradas", "text": "When the wind piles sand at the river's mouth, Hamilcar marches his army across and outflanks the rebels.", "lon": -54.019, "lat": -0.68}, {"year": -240, "title": "Battle of the Bagradas", "text": "A feigned retreat breaks Spendius's ranks: six thousand rebels die and two thousand are taken.", "lon": -54.4, "lat": -1.002}, {"year": -240, "title": "Naravas changes sides", "text": "The young Numidian prince Naravas joins Hamilcar with two thousand horsemen, promised his commander's daughter.", "lon": -58.973, "lat": -2.75}, {"year": -240, "title": "Victory in the hills", "text": "With Naravas, Hamilcar wins again; he offers prisoners a place in his army or freedom.", "lon": -57.068, "lat": -2.75}, {"year": -240, "title": "Gisco murdered", "text": "To stop desertions, the Gaul Autaritus and Spendius have Gisco and seven hundred prisoners mutilated and buried alive.", "lon": -53.828, "lat": -1.508}, {"year": -240, "title": "No truce", "text": "The rebels refuse to return the bodies and vow to kill every Carthaginian they take: the truceless war begins.", "lon": -53.904, "lat": -1.646}, {"year": -240, "title": "Sardinia mutinies", "text": "Carthage's garrison in Sardinia revolts too and kills its commander Bostar.", "lon": -53.028, "lat": -1.14}, {"year": -239, "title": "Utica and Hippo defect", "text": "The two cities kill five hundred Carthaginian soldiers, throw the bodies from the walls and join the rebels.", "lon": -54.095, "lat": -0.312}, {"year": -239, "title": "Rome says no", "text": "Rome refuses Utica's offer of surrender, lets its merchants supply Carthage and frees its prisoners.", "lon": -53.142, "lat": -1.462}, {"year": -239, "title": "Grain from Syracuse", "text": "King Hiero of Syracuse, fearing a Rome without rivals, sends Carthage everything it asks for.", "lon": -53.104, "lat": -1.324}, {"year": -239, "title": "Carthage under siege", "text": "Mathos and Spendius blockade Carthage itself from Tunis and Utica.", "lon": -53.371, "lat": -1.324}, {"year": -239, "title": "Hamilcar takes command", "text": "Hanno and Hamilcar cannot work together; the army chooses Hamilcar.", "lon": -53.218, "lat": -1.416}, {"year": -239, "title": "Cutting the supply lines", "text": "Hamilcar and Naravas raid the rebels' supply routes from the interior.", "lon": -54.972, "lat": -2.428}, {"year": -238, "title": "The siege is lifted", "text": "Starving in their own lines, the rebels abandon the blockade of Carthage.", "lon": -53.333, "lat": -1.508}, {"year": -238, "title": "Spendius takes the field", "text": "Spendius leads some fifty thousand men into the open country, shadowed by Hamilcar.", "lon": -53.638, "lat": -2.52}, {"year": -238, "title": "Trapped at the Saw", "text": "Hamilcar traps them at the Saw, a ridge of hills whose site is unknown; they eat their prisoners and slaves.", "lon": -52.685, "lat": -2.98}, {"year": -238, "title": "Hamilcar's terms", "text": "Spendius, Autaritus and eight others come to negotiate; Hamilcar names them as the ten he will keep.", "lon": -52.57, "lat": -3.118}, {"year": -238, "title": "Massacre at the Saw", "text": "Leaderless, the trapped army is destroyed by elephants and infantry: more than forty thousand die.", "lon": -52.799, "lat": -2.842}, {"year": -238, "title": "Spendius crucified", "text": "Hamilcar's army besieges Tunis and crucifies Spendius before its walls.", "lon": -53.714, "lat": -1.646}, {"year": -238, "title": "Hannibal crucified", "text": "A night attack from Tunis captures the general Hannibal, crucified on Spendius's cross with thirty nobles.", "lon": -53.561, "lat": -1.83}, {"year": -238, "title": "Generals reconciled", "text": "Carthage's council forces Hanno and Hamilcar to make peace and fight together.", "lon": -53.18, "lat": -1.324}, {"year": -237, "title": "Battle of Leptis", "text": "Near Leptis Minor, the joint army wipes out Mathos's last force; Mathos is captured.", "lon": -51.046, "lat": -6.798}, {"year": -237, "title": "Mathos's end", "text": "Mathos and his men are led through Carthage and tortured to death by the crowd.", "lon": -53.218, "lat": -1.37}, {"year": -237, "title": "Utica surrenders", "text": "Utica, besieged by Hanno, surrenders on Carthage's terms.", "lon": -54.171, "lat": -0.404}, {"year": -237, "title": "Hippo surrenders", "text": "Hippo Acra, besieged by Hamilcar, surrenders.", "lon": -54.895, "lat": 0.562}, {"year": -237, "title": "Rome takes Sardinia", "text": "Rome accepts the island from the mutineers and threatens war; Carthage gives up Sardinia and pays 1,200 talents more.", "lon": -53.066, "lat": -1.232}, {"year": -237, "title": "Hamilcar sails for Spain", "text": "Hamilcar leads an army to Spain, taking his nine-year-old son, Hannibal.", "lon": -53.142, "lat": -1.6}, {"year": -236, "title": "A new empire", "text": "Hamilcar fights in southern Spain, building the silver-rich empire that will pay for Hannibal's war.", "lon": -53.18, "lat": -1.37}], "eras": [[-241, -241, "The Unpaid Army"], [-240, -239, "The Truceless War"], [-238, -237, "Hamilcar's Reckoning"], [-236, -236, "The Road to Hannibal"]], "refLine": null, "metrics": [{"label": "Held by Carthage", "stages": [1, 3, 5]}, {"label": "Held by the rebels", "stages": [2]}], "chartNote": "Share of the area of present-day Tunisia, by who controlled most of each governorate; today's boundaries stand in for an ancient countryside the sources barely describe. Dates follow Polybius and Hoyos and may be a year out. A simplification: the desert south was never part of the war.", "chartTitle": "Who held Carthage's Africa", "shares": [[0.5079, 0.4873, 0.0048, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], [0.487, 0.0998, 0.3694, 0.0209, 0.023, 0.0], [0.487, 0.098, 0.3923, 0.0209, 0.0018, 0.0], [0.487, 0.0998, 0.3231, 0.0209, 0.0048, 0.0644], [0.487, 0.0998, 0.0, 0.0209, 0.0, 0.3923], [0.487, 0.0998, 0.0, 0.0209, 0.0, 0.3923]], "seaTile": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,", "theme": {"--sea": "#14304A", "--sea-deep": "#0B1D2E", "--shade": "10,20,30", "--neighbor": "#2E4556", "--neighbor-edge": "#5B7385", "--glaze": "#F8F2E8", "--gold": "#B9863F", "--gold-bright": "#DDAE62", "--accent": "#6B1F4E", "--accent-hover": "#842862", "--ink": "#1E1A22", "--ink-muted": "#625A66", "--paper": "#F2EBDF", "--font-display": "'Marcellus', 'Noto Serif', 'DejaVu Serif', 'Noto Sans CJK JP', Georgia, serif", "--font-body": "'Cardo', 'Noto Serif', 'DejaVu Serif', 'Noto Sans CJK JP', Georgia, serif", "--cobalt": "#14304A", "--cobalt-deep": "#0B1D2E", "--wine": "#6B1F4E"}}